# The SigmaHQ/sigma revision that the detection-verification baselines in this
# directory were computed against. CI checks out exactly this commit, so the
# regression gate is reproducible: a green run stays green until someone
# deliberately moves the pin, rather than reddening on an unrelated pull request
# because upstream merged a rule overnight.
#
# Falling behind upstream is a real thing to know about — it is just not a thing
# that should block a contributor. .github/workflows/sigma-drift.yml runs these
# same baselines against upstream main on a schedule, so drift surfaces there.
#
# The pin and the baselines are one fact stored twice, and they must move
# together. Never hand-edit this file:
#
#     scripts/sync-sigma.sh --bump latest    # or a specific 40-hex commit id
#
# scripts/sync-sigma.sh --check runs on every pull request and fails if this
# value and the `sigma_ref` recorded inside each .ci/verified-<platform>.json
# have drifted apart.
